@@ -8912,3 +8912,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-11: ARC-AGI-3 BREAK A LEVEL WALL via EXPLORE-FIRST per-level re-induction (the exp4003 wall-hold fix; +1..+n levels per the MANDATORY Incremental-Progress rule): exp4003 held the walls because it re-induced per-level rules WITHOUT observing per-level dynamics first. Apply the exp4004 explore-first method that SOLVED su15: per stalled level, (1) a bounded active-exploration phase OBSERVES the per-level transitions, (2) induce the level rule from the OBSERVED transitions, (3) GAP-4 verifier-validate the candidate against held-out transitions, (4) commit actions ONLY if it validates. Target the lp85 & sc25 L2 walls and r11l L4 (whichever validates). STOP each game at the first level that fails (NOT all levels). Report new_levels_this_task + ACCURACY_total_levels_solved (raise PAST the banked 5) + verifier_validated_count + actions_saved_vs_openloop. Real-env-confirmed; holding at 5 with WHY each wall stalled is an honest no-advance complete. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: level_walls_hold_lp85_L2_no_verifier_validated_level_up_candidate_after_explore_first_observation_sc25_L2_no_verifier_validated_level_up_candidate_after_explore_first_observation_r11l_L4_no_verifier_validated_level_up_candidate_after_explore_first_observation_total5; results/experiment_4014_break_level_wall_explore_first.json
 - 2026-06-11: FIFTH ARC-AGI-3 game first-solve via the PROVEN explore-first method (raises games-solved 4->5): exp4004 solved a 4th game (su15) with the explore-first ORDER -- (1) active-exploration OBSERVES transitions, (2) induce the mechanic + goal predicate from OBSERVED transitions, (3) GAP-4 verifier as action-pruner on the grounded model. Apply the SAME proven method to the next-easiest NON-SPATIAL game from the remaining candidates (tn36-ef4dde99 / dc22 / the other non-spatial survivors -- pick by smallest L0 baseline_actions + directly-observable goal; AVOID vc33's PSPACE spatial trap). A 5th distinct solved game raises generalization 4->5. Real-env-confirmed. Report ACCURACY_levels_solved + game_solved + first_solve_at_action + actions_vs_baseline + exploration_actions_used. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: fifth_game_solved_tn36-ef4dde99_at_action7; results/experiment_4015_fifth_game_explore_first.json
 - 2026-06-11: ArcMemo SOLVE-transfer v4 (self-learning MANDATE; extends the exp4005 14->10 win to .371's NEW content): exp4005 showed concept-memory-seeded solving cut actions 14->10 on new content. This tests whether the SAME concept memory makes THIS milestone's new content cheaper: the higher level from exp4014 OR the 5th game from exp4015 (or a re-held-out solved level if neither advanced). Two arms at equal perception: (A) cold-start (no memory), (B) concept-memory-seeded (retrieve+try the banked concepts: 'select-then-place' r11l, 'permute-set' lp85, 'pattern-match-then-navigate' sc25, 'lattice-step-toward-target' su15 + any new concept). Does retrieving banked concepts reduce ACTIONS/ATTEMPTS to solve genuinely NEW content vs cold-start? Tier-2 constraint memory (research-program.md) compounding across the milestone's own progress. POSITIVE CONTROL: the target must share structure with >=2 banked concepts (else transfer is impossible by construction; FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK). (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: arcmemo_solve_transfer_v4_11to7_actions; results/experiment_4016_arcmemo_solve_transfer_v4.json
+- 2026-06-11: Hardware continuity (consolidated): SSH/USB-reachability + terminal-state check for each attached board -- KV260 (ssh kria, xmutil listapps), GateMate (openFPGALoader -c dirtyJtag --detect), PolarFire (ssh polarfire). Record per-board reachability + the next concrete forward step; no bitstream redesign. Per north-star §3, KV260 is the sovereignty story to drive to terminal then freeze; GateMate/PolarFire are opportunistic. Per CLAUDE.md KV260 SSH-Not-SD-Card Discipline: NEVER use the host SD-card block device as a KV260 precondition (SSH-reachability is the ONLY valid KV260 precondition). Use DISTINCT wall-clock timers per board (the exp3866 TAUTOLOGY corrigendum). (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=complete: hardware_continuity_4017_kvreachable_overlay_absent_gmblocked_gatemate_unreachable_pfreachable_ssh_continuity_recorded; results/experiment_4017_hardware_continuity.json
